# CLAUDE.md - Agent Instructions for {{COMPANY_NAME}} Knowledge Base

## What This Repo Is

This is {{COMPANY_NAME}}'s LLM knowledge base, compiled from Confluence.
It contains {{PAGE_COUNT}} pages across {{SPACE_COUNT}} Confluence spaces,
organized into a searchable, queryable wiki.

{{ACCESS_NOTE}}

## Directory Structure

```
{{REPO_NAME}}/
  ckb-config.yaml          # Configuration
  raw/                     # Original markdown pages from Confluence
  wiki/                    # Compiled knowledge base organized by category
    _index.md              # Master index - start here
    _summaries.md          # One-line summary of every page
{{CATEGORY_TREE}}
    spaces/                # Per-space summaries
  output/                  # Q&A answers and reports
  confluence_kb/           # Python CLI source
```

## CLI Commands

Activate the environment first:
```bash
source venv/bin/activate
```

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `ckb status` | Show KB stats |
| `ckb search "TERMS"` | Full-text search |
| `ckb query "QUESTION"` | LLM-powered Q&A (needs API key or Claude Pro/Max) |
| `ckb compile --fast` | Recompile wiki (heuristic, no LLM) |
| `ckb compile` | Full LLM recompile |
| `ckb interactive` | Interactive Q&A session |
| `ckb lint` | Health checks |

## How to Search

1. Read `wiki/_summaries.md` to scan all pages quickly
2. Use `ckb search "your query"` for ranked results
3. Read full articles at `wiki/{category}/{slug}.md`
4. For complex questions: `ckb query "your question"`

## Agent Contribution Protocol

When you learn new information about {{COMPANY_NAME}}, write it to the wiki:

1. Create `wiki/{category}/{slug}.md` with frontmatter:
```yaml
---
title: "Descriptive Title"
category: {category}
compiled_at: "{ISO timestamp}"
source_page_id: "agent-contributed"
source_space: AGENT
---
```

2. Use clear headers and factual content
3. Categories: {{CATEGORIES_LIST}}
4. Mark agent content with `source_space: AGENT`
5. Do not modify files in `raw/` — only edit `wiki/`

## Authentication

LLM features work automatically in Claude Code (Pro/Max subscription).
Otherwise set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` environment variable.
